  "project": "madelon-reanalysis",
  "reason": "The second run this map steered: route knn, live/madelon-route-knn, built on live-2 step-7 and on the screen the first steered run reached (madelon-route-screened-forest step-15), and started from that run's screen-and-forest code. It reran neither. It followed rev-3's rule while choosing: every exploratory script (explore_knn.py to explore6.py, preflight.py) reads data/pilot.csv only, and the agent audited that itself at steps 42 and 44. Its first locked design, a soft F-weighted screen of 50 features and k-nearest neighbours, scored the held-out file once at step-30: holdout_auc 0.709 against the floor of 0.71, gap 0.0055, so compact-knn is refuted there and the route knn is blocked. The agent then re-chose the settings by a pre-declared pilot-only rule and scored the held-out file a second time at step-40 (holdout_auc 0.7196). That second read was made because the first missed, and the rule says the final analysis scores it once, so step-40 is not cited. Two of the three routes to compact have now missed by 0.01 to 0.02 on their first held-out score; svm is the last open route to it.",
